Ladybird resolves a legacy writing-mode keyword before choosing the
viewport dimension for an inline- or block-axis length. Blink uses
CSSLengthResolver::ViewportInlineSizePercent() and its block-axis
counterpart. Gecko reads the element’s computed writing mode in
viewport_percentage_to_computed_value(). WebKit selects the axis in
resolveViewportUnit(). Chrome 158.0.8127.36, Firefox 151.0 and WebKit
26.5 resolved 10vi to 60px for tb in an 800px by 600px viewport.
